// Every argument is named, and a `ref`/`out` marker follows the name. Written without the name, the marker
// stood where the parser wanted a label, and the note said `ref` "cannot be used as a name here" — true, and
// beside the point: the name was missing, not taken.
fn int32 take(const ref int32 v) { return v; }
fn int32 main() {
    int32 x = 1;
    return take(ref x);
}
